From: Pyra kernel work <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: ti: aess: do not advertise 44.1 kHz

The three AESS playback front ends -- MM1, Tones and the low-power MM1 LP
that PulseAudio uses -- offer SNDRV_PCM_RATE_44100. The engine cannot play
it.

44.1 kHz on this hardware is not a per-port setting. The whole ABE changes
timebase: omap_aess_write_event_generator() slows the event counter from
2048 to 2228 (32768 * 6000 / 88200), so the schedule, and with it the
McPDM frame rate, drops from 96 kHz to 88.2 kHz. That is why omap-mcpdm.c
advertises 88200 alongside 96000 -- the only reason it ever would.

That path is written and never taken. EVENT_44100 is defined in aess-fw.h
and handled in omap_aess_write_event_generator(), and no caller anywhere in
sound/soc/ti ever passes it; the only requests are EVENT_TIMER at probe and
in omap_aess_wakeup(), and EVENT_STOP. Meanwhile
omap_aess_pcm_hw_params() does pass params_rate() down, so
omap_aess_connect_irq_ping_pong_port() duly selects the 44.1 kHz ping-pong
task (aess_port.c, tsk_freq[2]).

So a 44.1 kHz stream was configured for 44.1 kHz and clocked at 48 kHz: it
plays 8.84% fast, about a semitone and a half sharp. With
avoid-resampling = yes and alternate-sample-rate = 44100 in the PulseAudio
configuration -- the shipped default -- every 44.1 kHz file, which is to
say most music, went down that path.

Advertise 48 kHz only, so the constraint is enforced where userspace can
see it instead of depending on a daemon's configuration, and let userspace
resample. Restoring 44.1 kHz means converting the timebase switch, the
twl6040 PLL and the McPDM back end together, which is a separate piece of
work.
---
--- a/sound/soc/ti/aess/omap-aess-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/ti/aess/omap-aess-dai.c
@@ -1171,7 +1171,8 @@
 			.stream_name = "MM1 Playback",
 			.channels_min = 1,
 			.channels_max = 2,
-			.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_44100 | SNDRV_PCM_RATE_48000,
+			/* 48 kHz only; see "MMLP Playback" below. */
+			.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_48000,
 			.formats = SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE |
 				   SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE,
 		},
@@ -1233,7 +1234,8 @@
 			.stream_name = "Tones Playback",
 			.channels_min = 1,
 			.channels_max = 2,
-			.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_44100 | SNDRV_PCM_RATE_48000,
+			/* 48 kHz only; see "MMLP Playback" below. */
+			.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_48000,
 			.formats = SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE |
 				   SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE,
 		},
@@ -1271,7 +1273,23 @@
 			.stream_name = "MMLP Playback",
 			.channels_min = 2,
 			.channels_max = 2,
-			.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_44100 | SNDRV_PCM_RATE_48000,
+			/*
+			 * 48 kHz only. 44.1 kHz is not something the port can be
+			 * told about on its own: the whole engine changes timebase
+			 * with it. TI's design slows the event generator from
+			 * counter 2048 to 2228 -- 32768 * 6000 / 88200 -- so the
+			 * schedule, and with it the McPDM frame rate, drops from
+			 * 96 to 88.2 kHz, which is why omap-mcpdm.c advertises
+			 * 88200 at all. omap_aess_write_event_generator()
+			 * implements that as EVENT_44100 and nothing ever asks for
+			 * it, so a 44.1 kHz stream was configured on the 44.1 kHz
+			 * ping-pong task (aess_port.c) and then played out on the
+			 * 48 kHz schedule: 8.84% fast, about a semitone and a half
+			 * sharp. Advertise what actually works and let userspace
+			 * resample, until the timebase switch, the twl6040 PLL and
+			 * the McPDM back end are converted together.
+			 */
+			.rates = SNDRV_PCM_RATE_48000,
 			.formats = SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE |
 				   SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE,
 		},
